From 8b2df2e934f8ba5cfaa17ebc4733e9ccfae27983 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Season Tempo Build <claude@seasontempo.local>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 17:16:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Budget delete: the confirmation was never rendered

Clicking Delete on a budget line did nothing visible. No modal, no error, no
change to the row.

FinanceClient passed confirmingDelete, onCancelDelete, onConfirmDelete and
deleteError to BudgetTab. BudgetTab's parameter list did not name them, so they
were dropped there and never reached BudgetSection, whose own
`confirmingDelete = null` default then made the comparison against
`budget:<id>` permanently false.

The click handler fired and the state changed. Nothing rendered it. Nothing was
hidden, off-screen or behind a z-index, which is why the earlier
scroll-into-view change had no effect on it at all.

The confirmation is now a modal rather than an inline block. Inline is right in
a drawer, where it sits beside what it is about; inside an expandable table it
is unmounted the moment the coach collapses the category, stranding the state.
The modal renders once at section level, outside every group, and resolves the
row across all categories so a collapsed one still works. Escape and a backdrop
click cancel, neither while the request is in flight.

Convention check 4j is added for the class of fault: a prop a parent passes must
be destructured by the child. Like 4i, this is a default value turning a wiring
mistake into a silently wrong screen instead of an error.
